  "rootRulingMA1": {
    "kind": "Root ruling, not an owner decision",
    "source": "E:/Projects/Personal/MekStation-wt/_receipts/carry-forward.md",
    "section": "2026-10-28 Root ruling: A2 gating mutant MA1 survived (assertion removal)",
    "verbatim": "## 2026-10-28 Root ruling: A2 gating mutant MA1 survived (assertion removal)\n\nFacts (from _reports/2026-10-28/a2-impl/STOPPED.json, head 04d9f2d42): GREEN built run 26/26 on the first attempt. MA1 removes the actor reply id from `ids = new Set([acted.reply.event?.id, seen.frame.event.id])` in concurrent-first-sockets. It passed 26/26. The worker correctly found it is not equivalent, and stopped.\n\nRoot reading: MA1 deletes an assertion. On a correct product the actor's reply and the guest's delivery carry the same event id, so no run on an unmutated server can kill it. This is a gap in how the mutant was specified at admission, not a missing harness check. The fault classes differ:\n- A MatchHostRegistry race (two hosts for one match) is caught before the equality check: the guest's intentId-correlated waitFor times out.\n- The equality check exists only for id divergence: the guest receives the same intent's event under a different id than the actor's reply.\n\nRuling: discharge MA1 as a paired (combined) mutant, the method CF-A2M-1 already asks for on R6.\n1. Build one image with a product mutant PA1, so that the guest-visible event id diverges from the actor's reply id for the same intent.\n   - It goes at the narrowest seam (for example the publish/broadcast envelope in ServerMatchHostPublication.ts or ServerMatchHostCommandResults.ts).\n   - If it breaks an earlier row, scope it to the cfs match. Disclose the scoping.\n   - PA1 is scratch only. It is never committed and is restored byte-exact afterwards.\n2. Run the unmutated A2 harness against PA1. Required: concurrent-first-sockets fails on the named check \"concurrent first sockets conflicted\", with two ids. A failure at an earlier row or a different check does not count.\n3. Run the MA1 harness against the same PA1 image, without a rebuild. Required: concurrent-first-sockets passes, which shows MA1's deleted assertion was the only thing that caught PA1.\n4. Record MA1 as killed in combination, with PA1 as its witness, and disclose it as such. It is not a plain kill.\n\nIf no single-seam PA1 can make the ids diverge without breaking the build, stop and report. Root will then rule MA1 a disclosed survivor (R6 precedent). MA2-MA5 continue under the unchanged rule: a survivor stops the unit unless shown equivalent.\n",
    "verbatimSha256": "6f5f828d9a859272b167de4b66fd5eb5f4305fd93b561828d72746bc73b390b2"
  },
